- STATUS: FIRST line `PROGRESS B1497: b1497/hpsmpoc-customer-look-a11y HOLD`; `WORKING: <part>` lines; sections `## PRIOR WORK`, `## CLOSED WITH EVIDENCE`, `## BUILT`, `## HELD`, `## NOT RUN`, `## FOR THE RECORDS SEAT`, the change list, each proof (input, main, head), each check with predicate and counts. **LAST line on finish exactly `READY B1497: <head sha40>`** (equal to `git ls-remote` of the branch), else `HANDOVER B1497: next <part> <step> | done <parts>` or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>` (all three fire Tuesday's `status_watch.sh` case arm at line 56; the drafter fed sample lines of each to that arm and they fired, and `WORKING:` and `PROGRESS B1497:` lines did not). If every part closes with evidence or is held and nothing is built, end on `READY B1497: <main sha40>` and say "no branch pushed".
- Commits: plain ASCII, no B-numbers, no person names, no seat ids, no decision-card ids; one commit per part; end with your session's attribution line. `git push origin b1497/hpsmpoc-customer-look-a11y` only. Push as soon as a part's proofs are green.
- Shell: no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths; `git -C`; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count.

## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context start no new part; at about 75% stop at a safe boundary (files whole, every `next start` and Playwright process you started stopped by pid, the heavy lock removed, 9650-9659 free) and write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-11_B1497_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: the main sha, the closure lines written, the mutation diffs, the probe scripts' paths, the red and green counts per part), last line `HANDOVER B1497: next <part> <step> | done <parts>`, and end STATUS with the same line.

